        rules: {
          objective: 'Match tiles from hand to exposed table tiles to capture pairs; score by pip counts and red spots; highest total wins and others pay the difference.',
          gameplay: '1. Setup: Woodpile four tiles high; 16 tiles laid face up; each player draws hand (2 players: 12 each; 3 players: 8 each).\n2. Play: On your turn match one hand tile to an exposed tile (same pip total, or the 2-1 and 4-2 tiles Gee Joon together); collect the pair. A pair of 6-6 tiles may be laid immediately. Then draw one tile from woodpile; if it matches an exposed tile, collect it; else leave it face up.\n3. Matching: Identical tiles can form sets of three; fourth identical captures all.\n4. Scoring: Little fish (under 8 pips): 1 point per red spot, round up to multiple of ten. Big fish (8+ pips): 2 points per pip. Highest total wins; others pay winner the difference.',
          keyRules: [
            'Two tiles match when their pips have the same total; the 2-1 and 4-2 tiles (Gee Joon) match together',
            'Each turn: match one tile and collect pair, then draw one from woodpile and either collect or expose',
            'Little fish score by red spots (round up to ten); big fish score two points per pip',
            'Winner is highest score; others pay the difference to the winner',
          ],
